.TH LIBIMUD 3 "2026-08-05" "imud 1.8.2" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
libimud \- ABI-stable client library for the imud IMU daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <imud.h>
.PP
.BI "imud_t *imud_connect_stream(const char *" path );
.BI "imud_t *imud_connect_udp(int " port ", const char *" group );
.BI "imud_t *imud_connect_tcp(const char *" host ", int " port );
.BI "int     imud_read(imud_t *" h ", int " timeout_ms );
.BI "int     imud_reconnect(imud_t *" h );
.BI "const imud_data_t *imud_data(const imud_t *" h );
.BI "int     imud_fd(const imud_t *" h );
.BI "void    imud_free(imud_t *" h );
.BI "const char *imud_lib_version(void);"
.BI "unsigned imud_wire_version(const imud_t *" h );
.fi
.PP
Link with
.I \-limud
(pkg-config:
.IR libimud ).
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libimud
receives, validates, and decodes imud's binary telemetry so applications
do not have to know the wire format. Unlike the deprecated single-header
.I imud_client.h
(which pins the wire version and must be recompiled per packet revision),
libimud's interface is
.B ABI-stable
\(em applications compiled against it keep working across imud upgrades
without recompilation. The library is built and shipped with the daemon;
keep the two installed together.
.PP
.B imud_connect_stream
connects to the daemon's local AF_UNIX stream socket (lossless, the
recommended same-host path);
.I path
NULL or empty uses
.IR /run/imud/imud\-stream.sock .
.B imud_connect_udp
receives the high-rate binary UDP stream;
.I port
0 uses the default 10111, and a multicast
.I group
(224.0.0.0/4) is joined when given.
.B imud_connect_tcp
(added in 1.6) connects to a daemon's
.B [stream]
TCP listener
.RB ( tcp_enabled
in
.BR imud.conf (5))
\(em the remote equivalent of
.BR imud_connect_stream :
the same lossless framed packets, over the network.
.I host
NULL or empty uses 127.0.0.1 (hostnames are resolved, IPv4);
.I port
0 uses the default 10112. All three return NULL on error with
.I errno
set.
.PP
.B imud_read
waits up to
.I timeout_ms
milliseconds (negative blocks indefinitely) and returns
.B 0
when a new valid packet is available,
.B 1
on timeout, or
.B \-1
when the connection is lost \(em after which call
.B imud_reconnect
(retryable with backoff) or
.BR imud_free .
Malformed packets are discarded silently.
.PP
.B imud_data
returns the latest packet decoded into the
.B append-only
.I imud_data_t
view (attitude, heading \(em magnetic and true \(em rate of turn, heave and
heave rate, sea state (wave height/period, roll period), sensor triplets,
covariance, fusion diagnostics, timestamps, flags; see
.IR <imud.h> ).
The pointer is owned by the handle and updated in place by each successful
read.
.B imud_fd
exposes the descriptor for external select/poll loops: when readable, call
.BR imud_read (h,
0).
.SH ABI CONTRACT
.I imud_data_t
only ever grows: new members are appended, existing members never move,
change type, or disappear. Always access it through the pointer
.B imud_data
returns \(em do not copy the struct by value or persist
.IR sizeof(imud_data_t) .
Under those rules, binaries built against an older
.I imud.h
read their fields correctly from any newer
.IR libimud.so.0 .
A breaking change (none planned) would bump the SONAME.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/imud/imud-stream.sock
default daemon stream socket
.TP
.I /usr/include/imud.h
the public header, including the full imud_data_t field reference
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imud (8),
.BR imud.conf (5)
.PP
The wire-format spec and the version-pinned single-header alternative are in
.IR /usr/share/doc/imud/ .
